      ":activity/steps": [
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186055590,
          ":step/content": {
            ":db/id": 17592186055974,
            ":tutorial/content": "We add two matrices by adding the corresponding entries. We can only do this if they have the same number of rows and columns, that is, they have the same dimensions.\n\nFor example, consider the matrices\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe see that both $A$ and $B$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices, so we can add them. The sum ${A} + {B}\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+1 & 3+0 \\\\ 2+0 & 4+(-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, the sum of two matrices is another matrix with the same dimensions.",
            ":tutorial/title": "Introduction"
          },
          ":step/next": {
            ":db/id": 17592186055591
          }
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186055591,
          ":step/content": {
            ":db/id": 17592186054648,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186054545,
              ":question/id": "45832301-e578-578d-8866-147b998a1c22",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4374",
              ":question/problem": "Calculate $A+B,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "We add the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-10 & -5+2 \\\\ -2+2 & 3-4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Adding Square Matrices"
          },
          ":step/next": {
            ":db/id": 17592186055594
          }
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186055592,
          ":step/content": {
            ":db/id": 17592186054649,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186054546,
              ":question/id": "fc4a66f3-5180-5ac0-bd4d-830196fa459a",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4375",
              ":question/problem": "Calculate $A-B,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "We subtract the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-B & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2-0 & -1-(-1) \\\\ -1-2 & 0-(-1) \\\\ 3-(-1) & 2-3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Subtracting Matrices"
          }
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186055593,
          ":step/content": {
            ":db/id": 17592186055975,
            ":tutorial/content": "We can subtract matrices in the same way that we add matrices: we subtract the corresponding entries. Again, we can only do this if they have the same number of rows and columns, that is, they have the same dimensions.\n\nFor example, consider the matrices\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe see that both $A$ and $B$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices, so, we can subtract them. The difference ${A} - {B}\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-1 & 3-0 \\\\ 2-0 & 4-(-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, the difference of two matrices is another matrix with the same dimensions.",
            ":tutorial/title": "Subtracting Matrices"
          },
          ":step/next": {
            ":db/id": 17592186055592
          }
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186055594,
          ":step/content": {
            ":db/id": 17592186054650,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186054547,
              ":question/id": "b77816bd-e128-5888-9973-97c51c99f7f0",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4396",
              ":question/problem": "Calculate ${A}+ {B},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "We add the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+(-2) & 3+(-3) & 1+1 & 0+1 \\\\ 2+1 & 4+(-2) & -1+3 & 2+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Adding Non-Square Matrices"
          },
          ":step/next": {
            ":db/id": 17592186055593
          }
        }
      ],
      ":activity/title": "Adding and Subtracting Matrices",
      ":db/id": 17592186054891
